+GDB EVIDENCE: the rc=101 CLI ICE on a closed stderr pipe
+=========================================================
+
+Toolchain: GDB 18.1 (pinned cache d66c5ac881e2), fastbuild lccc.
+Reproducer: 2000 `@ ;` lines (`/tmp/many-errors.c`); inferior stdout+stderr
+attached to a 4 KiB pipe whose reader closes after two lines -- exactly what
+`lccc bad.c 2>&1 | head -2` does. The reader is a Python thread so the close
+is deterministic (a shell `head` can exit after the compiler already filled
+the pipe buffer, which hides the EPIPE).
+
